    {
      "turn": 2,
      "doctor_question": "Have you always felt this need to keep moving, or is this something that has only started more recently?",
      "targeted_symptom": "duration",
      "patient_response": "Well, I suppose I've always been a bit of a doer, but... it's definitely gotten noticeably harder to manage recently. I'd say for about eight months now? Yes, right around eight months, because that’s when my youngest left for college. \n\nShe went all the way out to Oregon, which was quite a trek for us to get her moved in. We had to rent one of those massive moving vans, and let me tell you, my husband driving that thing through the mountain passes was absolutely terrifying. I kept telling him to pull over and let me drive, or at least slow down, but he is so stubborn when he gets behind the wheel of a large vehicle. We ended up having to stop at this quirky little motel in Northern California because it started pouring rain. \n\nBut anyway, since she moved out, the house has just become so much quieter. It used to be constantly full of teenagers and cello practice—she’s first chair, actually, she's been playing since she was six—and now it's just me and my husband. And I think without all that noise and chaos, the quiet just sort of... echoes? I don't know, but since the house got so quiet, I just can't seem to stay sitting down.",
