    {
      "turn": 3,
      "doctor_question": "When you feel this urge to stand up and move around, does it feel like you are doing it to relieve an internal sense of jitteriness or physical restlessness inside your body?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S010",
      "patient_response": "Yes, exactly, it's like this sort of... buzzing or jittery energy. If I can't actually get up and walk around, like when I'm sitting at my desk grading essays or when we're in church, I just end up shifting around in my seat so much. I'll catch myself tapping my foot, or clicking my pen over and over, and I really have to mentally remind myself to just settle down. \n\nWhich is terribly difficult during church lately, to be honest, because Reverend Davis has been doing this incredibly long sermon series on the minor prophets. And, well, he’s a lovely man, he really is, but his delivery is just so monotone. His wife, on the other hand, is an absolute delight. She brought this amazing lemon pound cake to the choir fundraiser last week. I used to bake a lot of pound cakes when the girls were little, but you really need a heavy cast-aluminum bundt pan for it to bake evenly, and my favorite one got all scratched up years ago when my husband tried to wash it with steel wool. I told him you can't use abrasive sponges on non-stick coating, but he never checks the labels on the cleaning supplies...",
