      "doctor_question": "Beyond the restlessness you've described, do you find that you spend a significant amount of your day worrying about various things—like your job, your family's health, or your finances—to the point where it feels difficult to control those thoughts?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "Worrying? No, not really. I mean, I care about my family, of course, and I want my students to do well, but I wouldn't say I'm overwhelmed by worry or anything like that. I don't sit around agonizing over the bills or whatever. My husband handles most of the finances anyway, which is a blessing because I've never been much good with numbers. \n\nThough speaking of numbers, the school district just changed our grading software again. They switched us to this new cloud-based system over the summer, and it is just the most convoluted interface you could possibly imagine. I spent three hours on the phone with the IT help desk last Tuesday just trying to figure out how to input the mid-term grades. The poor boy on the phone sounded like he was about twelve years old, and he kept asking me to clear my cache. I told him I did that, but he insisted I do it again. I swear, they hire these kids right out of high school and expect them to know how to fix everything. My oldest daughter's first job was actually at a call center for a catalog company, selling those fleece-lined slippers... they were so popular back in the late nineties, remember those? She hated it, but it paid for her first car. A little blue Honda Civic that smelled faintly of wet dog, even though we never owned a dog...",
