      "doctor_question": "Aside from the restlessness you've mentioned, have you been feeling persistently sad, down, or lacking interest and pleasure in the things you usually enjoy over these past eight months?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "Sad? Oh, heavens no. I haven't been feeling sad or down at all. I mean, I still love teaching, and I still enjoy my book club, even if I do have trouble sitting still through the discussions sometimes. But no, no loss of interest or anything like that. \n\nActually, speaking of book club, we're reading this fascinating biography of Eleanor Roosevelt right now. Did you know she used to write a daily newspaper column? Every single day! I can barely manage to write my weekly lesson plans without getting distracted by something else. Last week, I sat down to plan out our unit on the Roaring Twenties, and before I knew it, I was looking up vintage flapper dresses on the internet. They had such beautiful beadwork back then, didn't they? Real craftsmanship. You just don't see that kind of attention to detail in clothing anymore. Nowadays, everything is just mass-produced and falls apart after three washes. I bought a blouse from a department store just last month, wore it once, and a button popped right off while I was writing on the chalkboard. So embarrassing! I had to use a safety pin for the rest of the afternoon...",
